{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.IsospinSymmetryBreakingSu4Anomaly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.IsospinSymmetryBreakingSu4Anomaly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Isospin.doublet_degeneracy_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Isospin.doublet_degeneracy_split","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-symmetry-breaking-su4-anomaly.lean#L40-L50","doc":"**The Doublet Degeneracy Split.**\n\nThis theorem verifies that the application of the SU(4) categorical correction\nprecisely cancels the remaining disparity, yielding the exact mass closure across\nthe fundamental light isotopes.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Isospin.apply_su4_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Isospin.apply_su4_correction","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-symmetry-breaking-su4-anomaly.lean#L29-L38","doc":"**The SU(4) Dynamic Occupancy Correction.**\n\nThe recursive structure (CKRecursion) determines the isospin-symmetric baseline.\nThe fine structure of the mass spectrum—such as the ~0.76 MeV binding difference\nbetween ³H and ³He—is governed by the Seiberg-Witten residue of the SU(4) dynamic occupancy.\n\nInjecting the exact S_3/SU(4) representation differential splits the A=3 doublet degeneracy.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}